hat they  were thinking about doing is why didn't  they just do a bunch of these why didn't  they drop all of these right at launch  that would have been awesome well the  answer is twofold number one companies  generally would like to sell as few  variations of a single product as  possible as few skus as they can so if a  company could sell all their phones in  one color and one storage amount they  would that's why i see car companies  like bundling as many things as possible  into one option package is because they  don't want to have 75 different ways  they can make their car they just want  to make one so if you're a smartphone  company and you can just sell black and  white and maybe one other color then  that's what they'll do but the number  two answer right now is also that  smartphone companies are using alternate  colors as a press tool basically to  remind you about a smartphone that  already came out so there's something  you can call a press cycle every time a  new phone comes out there's a pretty  predictable spike of attention at the  beginning the height of sales and then  it sort of falls off in this long tail  as the device gets older maybe a drop in  price might bump it up again but for the  most part it'll never get that much  attention again but releasing a brand  new color of the same exact phone and  delaying it a couple months after that  release is obviously stirring up a brand  new press cycle it creates a new wave of  videos a new wave of articles brings a  little attention back to the phone and  at the end of the day we'll boost sales  oneplus does it samsung does it apple  does it almost everyone almost  everyone's guilty at some point of doing  this this special edition late release  smartphone and if you pay careful  attention to the way  apple does it  they specifically use new alternate  colors when a new product has the same  design or like the spec bump on the  inside so when they went from iphone 6  to iphone 6s the design of the phone was  exactly the same there's just a spec  bump like apple does so they added a  rose gold color so now you can tell who  has the new iphone you can't get the  iphone 6 in rose gold so you know that's  the new one and then when they went to  iphone 7 the design again was super  similar so we got this jet black version  so you can't get a jet black iphone 6 or  6s so you know that's the 7. even with  the new apple watch when they came out  with a new lte version they painted a  big red dot on the crown so you know  that person must have the new lte  version of the watch truly classic apple  and then this year rumors point to the  fact that there won't be a huge design  change with the next iphone 11 or  whatever they call it from the iphone 10  so same design maybe new sizes  but with that they're going to do new  colors so we've got these rumors of a  blue color and an orange color and a red  color to all launch with the new iphone  so you know you have the new one and the  thing is  i'm still pumped for it anyway like i  love it and i hate it i love it because  colored phones are actually really  exciting they look really cool  they're unique they're kind of personal  and everyone does it differently to make  themselves stand out there's about eight  or nine different red phone finishes  that have come out in the past couple  years and every single one of them has  different looks different hues different  reflectiveness different color shifting  my personal favorite i would say is  apple's product red probably followed  closely by oneplus new one and then  believe it or not the blackberry  passport in red but i'm so into all  these colored phones but i hate it  because i know it plays exactly  perfectly into the manufacturer's hands  they're gonna release a new alternate  color of this phone that they could have  probably released on day one but it's  gonna generate this new batch of  coverage and all these new videos and  articles and probably new sales now to  be fair i love what apple does with the  product red stuff not only with the  phones but with the cases and all that  stuff where they're working with a great  organization they're donating to aids  research i think more companies should  do stuff like this but the fact that the  phone comes out six months after the  original every time in red is pretty  hilarious at the end of the day though  i'm not gonna stop covering colored  phones in fact i'm gonna cross my  fingers for more of them i hope we get  all those new colored iphones i hope we  get all these new custom phones i missed  moto maker back in the days when you  could customize every little thing from  the material to the back of the phone to  the button colors and all of that that  was peak smartphone customization in my  opinion and that's where i want it to be  but until then i'll just keep crossing  my fingers  talk to you guys in the next video  thanks for watching  peace

